<title>UK: TABLE-ROYAL/SHELL Q2 PROFIT FLAT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-ROYAL/SHELL Q2 PROFIT FLAT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30</p>
<p>		    (billion stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Current cost net income excluding special items</p>
<p>				1.140		vs 1.187</p>
<p>Current cost net income including special items</p>
<p>				1.180		vs 1,188</p>
<p> Net income		 1.070		vs 1.183</p>
<p>Note - Analysts had forecast current cost before exceptional items in a range between 1.26 billion and 1.48 billion stg.  </p>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell Group is 60 percent owned by Royal Dutch Petroleum Co of the Netherlands and 40 percent by Britain's Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc.</p>
<p>		     (figures in millions unless stated)</p>
<p> Net proceeds		18,968		 vs 20,375</p>
<p> Gross profit		4,131		  vs 4,390</p>
<p> Operating profit	  2,416		  vs 2,435</p>
<p> Interest income	   130		    vs 173</p>
<p> Tax			   1,160		  vs 1,215</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
